#
# Counter-example for math:ApplicationExpressionShape: a math:ApplicationExpression
# applies TWO math:operator values (math:matrixProduct and math:tensorContraction),
# so it is ambiguous which operator the node invokes. Its two math:argumentSlot cells
# are otherwise well-formed — distinct indexes (0, 1), each with an expression — so the
# node fails ONLY on operator cardinality (sh:maxCount 1 on math:operator). Validation
# MUST emit shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding
# (math:ApplicationOperatorCardinality). Bound by ex:ecApplicationTwoOperators.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:badOpNode a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator math:matrixProduct , math:tensorContraction ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:opSlotA , ex:opSlotB .

ex:opSlotA a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:opExprA .
ex:opSlotB a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 1 ; math:slotExpression ex:opExprB .

ex:opExprA a math:MathematicalExpression .
ex:opExprB a math:MathematicalExpression .
